Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0016.
A hook for an out-of-tree quant plugin's L2 prefetch: after DeepseekV41LLMForCausalLM loads its weights, it hands the
model to vllm_exl3_moe.l2pf.register_decoder_layers when that plugin is installed, so the plugin can register per-layer
tensors it prefetches into L2 at its decode-time points (the fp32 mHC mix weights hc_attn_fn / hc_ffn_fn, 1.9 MiB each,
and the bf16 router gate, 3.75 MiB, with EXL3_L2PF_HC=1). Without the plugin, or with its prefetch off, nothing changes.
(V4.1 has its own model class in deepseek_v41/nvidia/model.py; V4's process_weights_after_loading is not on its path.)

--- a/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/model.py
+++ b/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/nvidia/model.py
@@ -1651,6 +1651,15 @@
         self.model.finalize_mega_moe_weights()
         self.model.finalize_mhc_broadcast_weights()
         self.model.finalize_mega_attn_weights()
+        # An out-of-tree quant plugin may prefetch per-layer weights into L2
+        # (vllm_exl3_moe: the mHC mix weights and router gates); a no-op
+        # unless that plugin is installed and its prefetch is switched on.
+        try:
+            from vllm_exl3_moe.l2pf import register_decoder_layers
+        except ImportError:
+            register_decoder_layers = None
+        if register_decoder_layers is not None:
+            register_decoder_layers(self.model)
 
     def get_expert_mapping(self) -> list[tuple[str, str, int, str]]:
         return self.model.get_expert_mapping()
